# The Boeing 747-400's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/747-400.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# Four CF6-80C2B1Fs, numbered one to four from the left, with neither mixture
# nor propeller: they are read by their N1, thirty per cent at idle and a
# hundred wide open. The outboard pair, engines one and four, stand for all
# four here. The flaps run from up to thirty degrees and the undercarriage
# retracts, so both are checks and not confirms. The model works its
# spoilers off the speedbrake lever alone, so nothing here reads a separate
# spoiler handle.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done, all doors shut, and both decks reported secure
confirm Auxiliary power unit running, and the four engines to be started in turn
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Thrust levers closed
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake lever down and stowed
confirm Parking brake set, beacon on, and the ground crew clear of all four engines

phase taxi
range propulsion/engine[0]/n1 28.0 45.0 Number one running, its thrust lever at idle
range propulsion/engine[3]/n1 28.0 45.0 Number four running, its thrust lever at idle
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 9.5 20.5 Take-off flap set, ten to twenty degrees
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Stabiliser trimmed for the take-off weight
confirm Brakes checked as it first moves, and the body gear steering seen to work
check velocities/vc-kts <= 25.0 Taxi at no more than twenty-five knots

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 9.5 20.5 Flaps twenty, the setting its field length is figured at
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 All five undercarriage legs down and locked
check propulsion/engine[0]/n1 >= 92.0 Number one at take-off thrust
check propulsion/engine[3]/n1 >= 92.0 Number four at take-off thrust
confirm Take-off briefed, transponder on, and the runway seen to be clear
check velocities/vc-kts >= 175.0 Rotate at 175 knots at the maximum take-off weight

phase climb
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up
check position/h-agl-ft >= 400.0 Climbing away from the runway
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up on the climb-out schedule
range velocities/vc-kts 240.0 330.0 Climb at 250 knots below ten thousand feet, then 320
check velocities/h-dot-fps >= 8.0 Going up at 500 feet a minute or better
confirm Landing lights off above ten thousand feet, and engine anti-ice as it is needed

phase cruise
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake stowed
range position/h-sl-ft 29000.0 45000.0 Level between FL290 and the ceiling of 45,100 feet
range velocities/mach 0.80 0.90 Cruising near Mach 0.85, inside the Mmo of 0.92
confirm Fuel burnt from the tanks in their scheduled order, and the trim tank watched

phase descent
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.50 Thrust levers back for the descent
range velocities/h-dot-fps -60.0 -5.0 Coming down between 300 and 3,600 feet a minute
range velocities/vc-kts 200.0 320.0 Down at 300 knots, and 250 below ten thousand feet
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps still up
confirm Altimeters set to the field's pressure passing the transition level
confirm Approach briefed, and both cabin decks told to make ready for landing

phase approach
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 All five legs down and locked
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 9.5 30.5 Flaps ten to thirty as the speed comes back
range velocities/vc-kts 150.0 210.0 Slowing through the flap speeds to the approach speed
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake lever stowed
check position/h-agl-ft <= 3000.0 Below three thousand feet and settled on the path
confirm Speedbrake armed, landing lights on, and the runway in sight

phase landing
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 24.5 30.5 Flaps thirty, or twenty-five in a strong wind
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 All five legs down and locked
range velocities/vc-kts 148.0 172.0 Over the threshold at about 155 knots
check position/h-agl-ft <= 60.0 Sixty feet and below, into the flare; the eyes ride high
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.15 All four thrust levers closed as the flare begins

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake lever down and the spoilers in
check propulsion/engine[3]/n1 <= 45.0 All four thrust levers at idle
check velocities/vc-kts <= 25.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
confirm Transponder to standby, landing lights off, and the auxiliary power unit on
